🔹 Program 8: Base Pointer Without a Virtual Function

📌 Description

This program demonstrates static binding using a base-class pointer.

The "display()" function is not declared "virtual". Therefore, when a base pointer points to a derived object, the base-class version of the function is called.

🎯 Concept Used

Static Binding

💡 Key Point

If a base-class function is not "virtual", the function call through a base pointer is resolved using the static type of the pointer.
